message.content:
This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   The user has been running an extensive, multi-day debugging/fixing session on a SharePoint SPFx SPA project (a rewrite of an older "HHHHQA" SPFx app, code-named "spa", split across `hhhh-shared-ui`, `hhhh-ui-library`, and `HHHHWorkspace` sibling packages under `/Users/smalsus/Desktop/SPA/` — this is the REAL project directory the IDE uses; `/Users/smalsus/office/spa/` is a stale, unrelated clone on branch `dev4` that the user has since deleted). Across the session the user requested, in order:
   - Understand and confirm the codebase structure (SPA vs old HHHHQA app).
   - Find exact component names for "relevant documents" in Portfolio Profile / PXC Profile (old and new).
   - Diagnose and fix a bug where Portfolio Profile's document counts didn't match the old page (12 vs 15 documents) — traced to an overly narrow file-type allowlist.
   - Diagnose and fix why navigating Project Overview → PXC Profile was fast/instant but Team Portfolio → Portfolio Profile was slow — with the explicit instruction to fix it by warming a SHARED cache at the SOURCE (whichever list page loads first), not by adding a new call on the Profile page itself. The user pushed back on an early "reconcile on Profile" instinct and insisted on the "fix at source" pattern used elsewhere in the app.
   - Diagnose and fix PXC Profile navigation showing incomplete data (missing breadcrumb, "Key Portfolio Items", "Worked Total" hours, "Add Existing Tasks" button) unless the page was hard-refreshed.
   - Verify a second AI tool's (Cursor's) independent analysis of the same PXC Profile bugs, correcting inaccuracies found via direct code verification.
   - Set up and use a local SPFx dev server (`gulp serve` via `npm run dev`) with the SharePoint "debug manifest" override to live-verify fixes, since the deployed App Catalog bundle doesn't reflect local source changes without a full build+deploy.
   - Fix Task Profile's "no callback on add/update/delete" complaint — specifically the "update" case (stale-data notification) and the "add" case (from the separate Create Task page, which never notified other pages at all), with an explicit additional instruction to "dyhan dena grouping sahi se ho" (pay attention that grouping/nesting is correct).
   - Fix "Add Workstream-Task" button in Task Profile's own sub-item table not reflecting newly created items locally, and a subsequent bug where the wrong popup (Task vs Workstream) opened depending on stale leftover state from a prior action — resolved via explicit user-confirmed answers to two clarifying questions (default-popup-when-nothing-selected = Workstream; post-create state = must be cleared, not set to the new item).
   - Produce a polished, plain-language End-of-Day report of all fixes, organized by page (explicitly: "just in which page do not write its child components" — i.e., organize by page name only, don't list internal component file names), published as a Claude Artifact.
   - Most recently: diagnose (not yet fix) a bug where, in Project Overview, searching for a project by title and then clicking the "+" expand icon shows no children (works fine when unfiltered) — with an explicit constraint: "fix there only not any place else" (the fix, when it happens, must be scoped to wherever the "+" icon's own click logic lives, not elsewhere) — followed by a request to compare against Team Portfolio's behavior for the same scenario, and finally the user's most recent explicit instructions (verbatim): "ek kaam karo tumhare pass poorana code bhi diya hia miane usme bhi ek baar check karo nad jab search kar ke plus icon pe click karte hai dhyan se accrodian ke arrow pe nhi plus icon pe jab click karte hai to wha pe console lagao ok" — i.e. (1) also check the equivalent old/legacy code, and (2) add `console.log` instrumentation specifically inside the "+" plus-icon's click handler (explicitly NOT the accordion/chevron arrow handler) in the shared table component, to aid live debugging.

   Throughout, the user communicates primarily in Hinglish/Hindi, is technically sharp and quick to correct wrong assumptions, occasionally uses profanity when frustrated (which I did not react to — I stayed professional, acknowledged mistakes plainly, and re-verified rather than getting defensive), and has a strong stated preference for: (a) diagnosing/checking before fixing when asked to "check karo" or "batao" first, (b) fixes being scoped precisely to where the user identifies the root belongs (and correcting me when I misdiagnose), (c) reusing/fixing shared "source of truth" caching mechanisms rather than adding new per-page fetches, (d) me verifying my own work via typecheck/build and, where possible, live browser testing rather than just claiming success.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - SPFx (SharePoint Framework) SPA built with React, TanStack (react-table) v8 tables, `sp-pnp-js` for SharePoint REST calls.
   - Monorepo-style sibling packages: `hhhh-shared-ui` (shared components/services, published as `@hochhuth-consulting/hhhh-shared-ui`, symlinked into `HHHHWorkspace/node_modules`), `hhhh-ui-library`, `HHHHWorkspace` (the actual SPFx solution/webpart).
   - In-memory, session-scoped caching layers in `globalCommon.tsx`: `masterListProcessedCache`/`masterListProcessedInFlight` (keyed by siteUrl + optional filter), `masterListFullRaw`/`masterListRawInFlight` (raw unfiltered dump per site), `sharedTaskStore`/`ensureSharedTasks`/`readSharedTasks` (site-tasks store with 'initial'/'above89' bands), all with "session-valid until full page reload, no time-based expiry."
   - "Seed" navigation pattern (`spaRowSeed.ts`): `setPortfolioSeed`/`getPortfolioSeed`/`clearPortfolioSeed`, `setTaskSeed`/`getTaskSeed`/`getAnyTaskSeed`/`clearTaskSeed` (newly added), `setPxcSeed`/`getPxcSeed`/`clearPxcSeed` — in-memory maps (NOT sessionStorage) used to instantly paint a profile page from the row the user clicked, skipping a fresh SharePoint fetch; explicitly cleared on full page reload.
   - Cross-page pub/sub for row changes (`spaRowChange.ts`): `notifyRowChange`, `subscribeRowChange`, `emitRowChange`, `mergeRowIntoTree`, `insertMasterRowIntoTree`, `removeRowFromTree`, `safeMergeRow`, `rowChangeId`, `inferRowList`.
   - `safeMergeRow` bug class: a plain `{...existing, ...incoming}` spread lets an `undefined`-valued key in a partial update payload silently wipe an existing populated field; fixed generally by only applying keys where `incoming[key] !== undefined`.
   - TanStack react-table specifics: `getExpandedRowModel`, `getFilteredRowModel`, `globalFilterFn`, `filterFromLeafRows: true`, `getSubRows: (row) => row?.subRows`, `getCoreRowModel().rowsById`, `row.getToggleExpandedHandler()`, `row.getCanExpand()`, `row.getIsExpanded()`, custom `hasCustomExpanded` prop-gated expand logic that manually pulls `subRows` from the CORE (unfiltered) row model and mutates row/row-model objects directly (not via React state) before calling `setExpanded(...)`.
   - SPFx local dev workflow: `gulp serve` on port 4321, `config/serve.json` `initialPage`, SharePoint's `?debug=true&noredir=true&debugManifestsFile=https://localhost:4321/temp/manifests.js` override, the "Allow debug scripts?" browser confirmation dialog, Node version constraints (`>=18.17.1 <19.0.0` etc., requiring `nvm use 18.18.0`), `npm run dev` → `scripts/dev-local.js` (watches sibling packages + runs `gulp serve` via `concurrently`).
   - Deployment reality: the live SharePoint site serves a built `.sppkg` from `sites/appcatalog/ClientSideAssets/<guid>/hhhh-spa-web-part_<hash>.js` — local `npm run build`/`tsc` changes do NOT reach it without a full `gulp bundle --ship && gulp package-solution --ship` + App Catalog deploy.
   - Artifact publishing workflow (`artifact-design` skill) for the EOD report — Google Fonts (IBM Plex Sans/Mono), CSS custom-property theming for light/dark via `:root`, `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` guarded `:not([data-theme="light"])`, and `:root[data-theme="dark"]`.

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`hhhh-shared-ui/src/HHHH-Directory/documents/TaskDocuments.tsx`**
     - Restored broad `includedTypes` allowlist (module-level const, ~line 27) to match old HHHHQA's list (docx, xlsx, pptx, pdf, doc, docs, xls, ppt, msg, aspx, link, xlsm, zip, figma, png, jpeg, jpg, gif, txt, csv, rar, url, fig, mp4, eml, rtf, eps, accdb, mp3, jfif, svg, mht, mhtml, xml, md, "", null, undefined).
     - Removed redundant type-filter inside `loadSubItemDocumentsTargeted()` (~line 772), since the REST query is already ID-scoped.
     - Parallelized the chunked document fetch (`Promise.all` over `chunks.map(...)` instead of sequential `for` loop), ~lines 758-773.
     - (Earlier, in the now-irrelevant `dev4`/stale-checkout phase, also fixed an async-race in `LoadAllSiteTasks` — not carried forward once the real `main` checkout was found; the SAME conceptual fix was NOT re-verified as still needed there since focus shifted to other bugs.)

   - **`hhhh-shared-ui/src/HHHH-SP-Code/services/globalCommon.tsx`**
     - Added `PortfoliosId` to `MASTER_TASK_UNIFIED_SELECT`'s Portfolios entry.
     - Added `TeamMembersId`, `ResponsibleTeamId` to the same select list.
     - Added `"TotalTime"` to `SHARED_TASK_SELECT` (with updated comment explaining PXC Profile's "Worked Total" now consumes it via the shared task store).
     - (Read but did not modify) `GetPXCData`, `GetServiceAndComponentAllData`, `masterListProcessedCache`, `ensureSharedTasks`/`readSharedTasks`/`resolveVisibleTaskSites`, `fetchMasterListPXCRaw`/`fetchMasterListCSFRaw`, `ensureMasterListFullDump`.

   - **`hhhh-shared-ui/src/HHHH-SP-Code/services/spaRowChange.ts`**
     - Generalized `safeMergeRow` to skip any `incoming` key whose value is `undefined` before applying it onto `next`, in addition to the pre-existing `subRows`/`PercentComplete` special-case guards. (Note: a later system-reminder showed the dist had ALSO gained a `fromRestLookup` helper — apparently added by the user/Cursor externally — which I reviewed and endorsed as a good complementary fix, not something I authored or need to revert.)

   - **`hhhh-shared-ui/src/HHHH-SP-Code/services/spaRowSeed.ts`**
     - Added new exported function:
       ```ts
       export function clearTaskSeed(taskId: number | string | null | undefined): void {
         const id = Number(taskId);
         if (!id || Number.isNaN(id)) return;
         const prefix = `${id}::`;
         Array.from(taskSeeds.keys()).forEach((key) => {
           if (key.startsWith(prefix)) taskSeeds.delete(key);
         });
       }
       ```
       Mirrors existing `clearPortfolioSeed`/`clearPxcSeed`, which task seeds previously lacked entirely.

   - **`hhhh-shared-ui/src/HHHH-UI/tables/RadimadeTable.tsx`**
     - Added `pushUnderCurrentRootItem(row)` helper (module/component-scope, right before `Call`):
       ```ts
       const pushUnderCurrentRootItem = (row: any): boolean => {
         const rootId = SelectedProp?.SelectedItem?.Id ?? SelectedProp?.SelectedItem?.ID;
         if (rootId == null) return false;
         const parentId =
           row?.ParentTask?.Id ?? row?.ParentTask?.ID ?? row?.ParentTaskId ??
           row?.Parent?.Id ?? row?.Parent?.ID ?? row?.ParentId;
         if (parentId == null || Number(parentId) !== Number(rootId)) return false;
         const newId = row?.Id ?? row?.ID;
         if (copyDtaArray.some((r: any) => (r?.Id ?? r?.ID) == newId)) return true;
         copyDtaArray = copyDtaArray.concat(row);
         return true;
       };
       ```
       Wired as an additional `else if (pushUnderCurrentRootItem(...))` fallback in both branches of `Call` (the `isPortfolioProfileCreatedTask` branch and the regular branch), before their existing final catch-all `else`.
     - In `Call()`, added (after `setIsOpenActivity(false); setIsOpenWorkstream(false); setActivityPopup(false);`, before the `isPortfolioProfileCreatedTask` branch):
       ```js
       setCheckedList({});
       if (SelectedItem) { SelectedItem.NoteCall = undefined; }
       if (SelectedProp?.SelectedItem) { SelectedProp.SelectedItem.NoteCall = undefined; }
       ```
     - In `Createbutton()`, both `checkedList?.TaskType === undefined` branches (the AllAwt-inner-else branch and the top-level regular-else branch) changed from `setIsOpenActivity(true)` to `setIsOpenWorkstream(true)`, each now also doing `if (SelectedItem) SelectedItem.NoteCall = undefined;` before opening.
     - Root cause found (module-level `let SelectedItem: any = {}` at line 111, synced via `SelectedItem = SelectedProp?.SelectedItem;` at line 213 — same object reference as `SelectedProp.SelectedItem`, never auto-resets): the `checkedList?.TaskType?.Id == 1`/`== 3` branches (untouched by me) do `SelectedItem.NoteCall = "Task";` which permanently taints the object; `CreateWS.tsx` (line ~204) checks `props?.selectedItem?.NoteCall == "Task"` to decide its own render mode, and falls back to `SelectedProp?.SelectedItem` whenever `checkedList` is empty.
     - **Most recently (in-progress, NOT YET APPLIED):** identified the "custom expand" (`hasCustomExpanded`) click handler at lines ~271-320 as the target for user-requested `console.log` instrumentation:
       ```js
       {hasCustomExpanded && <div>
           {((row.getCanExpand() &&
               row.subRows?.length !== row.original.subRows?.length) ||
               !row.getCanExpand() ||
               forceExpanded.includes(row.id)) &&
               row.original.subRows?.length ? (
               <div className="mx-1 flex items-center"
                   {...{
                       onClick: () => {
                           if (!forceExpanded.includes(row.id)) {
                               const coreIds = table.getCoreRowModel().rowsById;
                               row.subRows = coreIds[row.id].subRows;
                               const rowModel = table.getRowModel();
                               const updateRowModelRecursively = (item: any) => {
                                   item.subRows?.forEach((elem: any) => {
                                       if (!rowModel.rowsById[elem.id]) {
                                           rowModel.flatRows.push(elem);
                                           rowModel.rowsById[elem.id] = elem;
                                       }
                                       elem?.subRows?.length &&
                                           updateRowModelRecursively(elem);
                                   });
                               }
                               updateRowModelRecursively(row);
                               const temp = Object.keys(coreIds).filter(
                                   (item: any) =>
                                       item === row.id ||
                                       item.startsWith(row.id + ".")
                               );
                               forceExpanded = [...forceExpanded, ...temp];
                               setExpanded((prev: any) => ({
                                   ...prev,
                                   [row.id]: true,
                               }));
                           } else {
                               row.getToggleExpandedHandler()();
                           }
                       },
                       style: { cursor: "pointer" },
                   }}
               >
                   {!row.getCanExpand() ||
                       (row.getCanExpand() &&
                           row.subRows?.length !== row.original.subRows?.length)
                       ? <FaPlus style={{ fontSize: '10px', color: `${row?.original?.PortfolioType?.Color}` }} />
                       : row.getIsExpanded()
                           ? <FaMinus style={{ color: `${row?.original?.PortfolioType?.Color}` }} />
                           : <FaPlus style={{ fontSize: '10px', color: `${row?.original?.PortfolioType?.Color}` }} />}
               </div>
           ) : (
           ...
       ```
       This is DISTINCT from the plain accordion/chevron handler at ~line 264 (`row.getToggleExpandedHandler()` inside `getFirstColCell`) which the user explicitly said NOT to instrument.

   - **`HHHHWorkspace/src/pages/projectManagement/components/ProjectManagementMain.tsx`**
     - Added module-level `let ancestorLookupList: any = [];` right after `let AllFlatProject: any = [];` (~line 87-90).
     - In the seed branch of `GetMasterData` (`if (canUsePxcSeedTree) {...}`), right after `AllFlatProject = flattenPxcSeedTree(projectItem);`, added:
       ```js
       try {
         const ancestorDump = await globalCommon.GetPXCData(props?.props);
         ancestorLookupList = ancestorDump?.FlatProjectData || [];
       } catch (error) {
         ancestorLookupList = [];
       }
       ```
     - Changed Parent-resolution logic (Sprint and Cycle branches) from unconditional overwrite to:
       ```js
       const parentId = fetchedProject?.Parent?.Id ?? fetchedProject?.ParentId;
       fetchedProject.Parent =
         AllFlatProject?.find((data: any) => data?.Id == parentId) ||
         ancestorLookupList?.find((data: any) => data?.Id == parentId) ||
         fetchedProject.Parent;
       ```
     - Changed the seed-call-site condition (near end of `GetMasterData`) from:
       ```js
       if (loadtask == true && preTasksData?.length > 0 && projectData?.__fromPxcSeed !== true) {
         await LoadAllSiteTasks();
       }
       ```
       to:
       ```js
       if (loadtask == true && (projectData?.__fromPxcSeed === true || preTasksData?.length > 0)) {
         await LoadAllSiteTasks();
       }
       ```
     - Rewrote `LoadAllSiteTasks()`'s top (previously an unconditional early-return when `projectData?.__fromPxcSeed === true`) into an if/else:
       ```js
       const LoadAllSiteTasks = async function (isloading?: any) {
         if (!stillLive()) return;
         if (projectData?.__fromPxcSeed === true) {
           const visibleTaskSites = globalCommon.resolveVisibleTaskSites(
             await globalCommon.loadSmartMetadata(props?.props, 'Sites')
           );
           await globalCommon.ensureSharedTasks(props?.props, 'initial', visibleTaskSites);
           if (!stillLive()) return;
           AllSitesAllTasks = globalCommon.readSharedTasks({ listIds: visibleTaskSites.map((s: any) => s.listId) });
           AllSitesAllTasks.forEach((task: any) => {
             if (task.PercentComplete !== undefined && task.PercentComplete !== null) {
               task.PercentComplete = Math.round(task.PercentComplete * 100);
             }
           });
         } else {
           if (isloading !== false) setPageLoader(true);
           CSFdata = [];
           let AllMasterData: any = await globalCommon.GetServiceAndComponentAllData(props?.props, `Item_x0020_Type eq 'Component' or Item_x0020_Type eq 'SubComponent' or Item_x0020_Type eq 'Feature'`)
           if (!stillLive()) return;
           CSFdata = AllMasterData?.AllData;
           AllSitesAllTasks = preTasksData;
         }
         AllSiteTasksForRestrcture = globalCommon.deepCopy(AllSitesAllTasks);
         ...
       ```
       (rest of the function unchanged, now shared by both branches).

   - **`HHHHWorkspace/src/pages/taskprofile/components/TaskProfileComponent.tsx`**
     - Import line changed to add `clearTaskSeed`:
       `import { getTaskSeed, getAnyTaskSeed, seedMatchesId, clearTaskSeed } from "@hochhuth-consulting/hhhh-shared-ui/HHHH-SP-Code/services/spaRowSeed";`
     - `GetResult` signature: `const GetResult = async (notifyAfterSave?: boolean) => {...}`.
     - At the end (right after `setState({...Result: tempTask...})` and `updateResult(tempTask);`):
       ```js
       if (notifyAfterSave) {
         const savedId = rowChangeId(tempTask);
         if (savedId) {
           notifyRowChange({
             action: 'update',
             list: 'SiteTasks',
             id: savedId,
             siteType: tempTask?.siteType || listName,
             listId: tempTask?.listId,
             row: tempTask,
             source: 'task-profile',
           });
         }
       }
       ```
     - `CallBack("Save")` rewritten:
       ```js
       if (FunctionType == "Save") {
         counts++;
         const savedId = rowChangeId(state?.Result);
         if (savedId) {
           clearTaskSeed(savedId);
         }
         setState((prevState: any) => ({...}));
         setTimeout(() => {
           GetResult(true);
           setState((prevState: any) => ({...}));
         }, 1000);
       }
       ```
       (The premature `notifyRowChange(savedRow)` call that previously fired immediately with stale `state.Result` was removed.)

   - **`HHHHWorkspace/src/pages/createTask/components/CreateTaskComponent.tsx`**
     - Added import: `import { notifyRowChange, rowChangeId } from '@hochhuth-consulting/hhhh-shared-ui/HHHH-SP-Code/services/spaRowChange';`
     - After building `taskWithImages` (post `.items.add(item)` success, before `EditPopup(taskWithImages)`):
       ```js
       const newTaskId = rowChangeId(taskWithImages);
       if (newTaskId) {
         notifyRowChange({
           action: 'add',
           list: 'SiteTasks',
           id: newTaskId,
           siteType: taskWithImages?.siteType,
           listId: taskWithImages?.listId,
           row: taskWithImages,
           source: 'create-task',
         });
       }
       ```

   - **`hhhh-shared-ui/src/HHHH-UI/tables/GroupByReactTableComponents/GlobalCommanTable.tsx`** (current investigation, no edits yet)
     - Read extensively: `customGlobalSearch` (~line 494), `useReactTable({...})` config (~line 1017-1052, including `filterFromLeafRows: true`, `globalFilterFn: customGlobalSearch`, `getSubRows: (row) => row?.subRows`, no `getRowId` override), `getFirstColCell` (~line 260) containing both the standard expand (`hasExpanded`, line 264, `row.getToggleExpandedHandler()`) and the custom expand (`hasCustomExpanded`, lines 271-320, detailed above).
     - Confirmed no `getRowId` is set anywhere in this file (default positional/hierarchical row IDs are used).

   - **`HHHHQA/src/globalComponents/GroupByReactTableComponents/GlobalCommanTable.tsx`** (old/legacy code, just checked per user's latest request)
     - Confirmed via grep that it contains the SAME `hasCustomExpanded`/`coreIds`/`forceExpanded`/direct-mutation pattern (old lines ~205-251), meaning this expand mechanism was carried over unchanged from the legacy SPFx app, not newly introduced in the SPA rewrite.

   - **`HHHHWorkspace/src/pages/teamPortfolio/components/TeamPortlioTable.tsx`** and **`HHHHWorkspace/src/pages/projectmanagementOverviewTool/components/ProjectOverView.tsx`**
     - Confirmed both import/render `GlobalCommanTable`.
     - Confirmed `hasCustomExpanded: true` is passed in `ProjectOverView.tsx` at lines 521 and 903.
     - Confirmed `TeamPortlioTable.tsx` has a local `let hasCustomExpanded: any = true` (line 86) toggled true/false at various points (lines 1824, 1866, 2511, 2526, 2553) and passed as `hasCustomExpanded: hasCustomExpanded` (line 2568).

   - **Artifact:** `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-smalsus-office-spa/22568d4a-d2ad-46b2-aa09-d3e5115c9a05/scratchpad/spa-stability-log.html`
     - Published EOD report titled "SPA Stability Log" (favicon 🛠️), URL `https://claude.ai/code/artifact/f1df2370-7755-48cb-9555-ac3527061517`. Organized into log-entry sections per page (Portfolio Profile; PXC Profile; Team Portfolio + Project Overview; Task Profile + Create Task), each with plain-language "WAS/NOW" fix pairs. IBM Plex Sans/Mono via Google Fonts, teal accent (#1F6F78 light / #63C6CF dark), light+dark theme tokens per artifact-design skill rules.

4. Errors and fixes:
   - **Wrong working directory initially**: First edits were made in `/Users/smalsus/office/spa/hhhh-shared-ui` (branch `dev4`), which the user's IDE did NOT reflect. Root-caused via `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`/`git branch --show-current` (found `dev4`) and then a filesystem search (`find /Users/smalsus -maxdepth 5 -iname "hhhh-shared-ui"`) that located the REAL, IDE-used checkout at `/Users/smalsus/Desktop/SPA/hhhh-shared-ui` (branch `main`). Re-applied all relevant fixes there. User later deleted the `dev4` folder, confirming it's no longer relevant.
   - **Chrome browser tool multi-browser confusion**: `tabs_context_mcp` initially failed with "Multiple Chrome browsers are connected... none has been selected." Resolved via `AskUserQuestion` then `switch_browser` — first attempt connected to the WRONG browser (a different Microsoft/Anthropic account, hit an MFA/security prompt I correctly refused to click through); user said "no no you started in other one... ask to name it i will name it my name" — re-ran `switch_browser`, user connected the correct browser named "Utkarsh srivastva".
   - **`npm run dev` port conflict**: First `npm run dev` attempt failed with "Port 4321 is already in use" (a prior `gulp serve` was already running, started by the user or an earlier session). I did NOT kill it initially and instead reused it via the debug-manifest URL. When it later disappeared/stopped (`lsof` returned nothing), I safely started a fresh one.
   - **Wrong Node version for `gulp serve`**: `Error: Your dev environment is running NodeJS version v22.23.0 which does not meet requirements (>=18.17.1 <19.0.0 etc.)`. Fixed via `source ~/.nvm/nvm.sh && nvm use 18.18.0` before re-running `npm run dev`.
   - **`ENOSPC` disk-full errors**: Both a generic Bash tool-output write failure and a genuine webpack build failure (`ENOSPC: no space left on device, copyfile '.../dist/hhhh-spa-web-part.js' -> '.../release/assets/hhhh-spa-web-part.js'`) occurred when disk was at 95% (11GB/228GB free). I reported this to the user rather than deleting anything unilaterally, per the safety guidance against destructive actions on the user's machine without asking; a later retry succeeded once transient pressure eased.
   - **Stray `package-lock.json` diff**: An earlier failed `npx tsc` attempt (before finding the local `node_modules/.bin/tsc`) modified `hhhh-shared-ui/package-lock.json` unintentionally; I reverted it via `git checkout -- package-lock.json` before it could be mistaken for a real change. Later, a legitimate `npm install` (needed because `hhhh-shared-ui/node_modules` was empty) produced a small, expected lockfile version-normalization diff (0.3.37→0.3.41) that I flagged to the user as harmless/unrelated rather than silently leaving or reverting it.
   - **Misdiagnosis (self-corrected) — Team Portfolio search+expand behavior**: I first predicted Team Portfolio must have the identical "search hides children" bug as Project Overview (same shared `GlobalCommanTable`/`customGlobalSearch`/`filterFromLeafRows` code). User showed screenshots contradicting this. My FIRST live re-test (searching "Admin Tool") appeared to show only 2-3 individually-matching child rows, and I WRONGLY concluded this was consistent with pure per-row text matching (no special subtree preservation) — restating my "both pages are equally broken" claim. The user firmly corrected me: **"nhi admin tool ko tumne expan hi nhi. kiya plus icon pe click karo abhi maine band nhi kiya hai check akro"** (No — you didn't actually expand it, click the plus icon; I haven't closed it, check). I redid the test properly (explicitly collapsed then re-expanded C002) and found the FULL, correct, complete children set was restored — directly contradicting my prior conclusion. I explicitly and openly corrected myself to the user ("tumhara point sahi tha, meri last observation galat thi") rather than doubling down, then traced the REAL code-level mechanism (`hasCustomExpanded`'s core-row-model pull) that explains the correct behavior, and confirmed both pages DO enable this same custom mechanism (`hasCustomExpanded: true`), leaving the discrepancy currently traced to a NOT-yet-fully-confirmed data/rendering-level cause.
   - **User's most recent redirect**: after I proposed a "data reference stability" hypothesis, the user said (verbatim) they think it's a rendering issue and asked me to also check the old/legacy code and add `console.log` specifically inside the "+" plus-icon handler (explicitly not the accordion arrow) — I had just re-read the current code block to prepare this edit when the summary request interrupted.

